    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Musical Meteors</i> is a retro-style arcade game that mixes colorful pixel aesthetics, score-attack gameplay, and piano-inspired mechanics. Meteors are flying in from outer space -- each labeled with a musical note -- and your job is to destroy them by using either your computer keyboard or MIDI piano to press the matching note on the virtual piano.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Start off with a small range of notes and unlock each key as you play. The more meteors you destroy without missing a note, the bigger your combo streak grows, and the higher your score climbs. With an out-of-this-world soundtrack and special missions for those who want to test their skills,<i> Musical Meteors</i> is the complete piano-arcade game package.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You don't need a MIDI piano to play -- all features are fully functional using the computer keyboard -- but MIDI piano owners can plug one in to experience a whole new level of immersion as their piano<i> becomes</i> the controller!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong><i>NOTE:</i></strong><i> For best results, use a USB MIDI keyboard without interface hardware and ensure no other programs are trying to access the MIDI keyboard while playing.</i></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Features</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Computer keyboard and MIDI keyboard controls</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Score-attack, combo-centric arcade gameplay with progressing difficulty</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Additional missions/achievements for dedicated players</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Colorful, retro-inspired graphics and soundtrack</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Gameplay designed to help you develop piano dexterity</p></li></ul>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Musical Meteors</i> is a retro-style arcade game that mixes colorful pixel aesthetics, score-attack gameplay, and piano-inspired mechanics. Meteors are flying in from outer space -- each labeled with a musical note -- and your job is to destroy them by using either your computer keyboard or MIDI piano to press the matching note on the virtual piano.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Start off with a small range of notes and unlock each key as you play. The more meteors you destroy without missing a note, the bigger your combo streak grows, and the higher your score climbs. With an out-of-this-world soundtrack and special missions for those who want to test their skills,<i> Musical Meteors</i> is the complete piano-arcade game package.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You don't need a MIDI piano to play -- all features are fully functional using the computer keyboard -- but MIDI piano owners can plug one in to experience a whole new level of immersion as their piano<i> becomes</i> the controller!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong><i>NOTE:</i></strong><i> For best results, use a USB MIDI keyboard without interface hardware and ensure no other programs are trying to access the MIDI keyboard while playing.</i></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Features</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Computer keyboard and MIDI keyboard controls</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Score-attack, combo-centric arcade gameplay with progressing difficulty</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Additional missions/achievements for dedicated players</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Colorful, retro-inspired graphics and soundtrack</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Gameplay designed to help you develop piano dexterity</p></li></ul>",
    "short_description": "Blast meteors in this retro-style arcade game with a musical twist! Use your keyboard or plug in a MIDI piano to methodically (and melodically) destroy the oncoming meteors. Shoot for high scores, rack up massive combos, and develop your piano dexterity along the way!",
